    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.20.0</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:21:33 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22000</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.20.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Every project is now a pond. The sidebar says Ponds, and Create says New pond.</li><li>Invite is the only step to share a pond; it signs you in first if you are signed out.</li><li>Ponds are on for everyone. A pond only you can see stays on this Mac until you invite someone.</li><li>Create opens a page in the workspace to start work, add a project or join a pond.</li><li>You can add a profile photo to your Squeak account in Settings › Account.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.19.1</h4><ul><li>The Mac menu at the top of the sidebar shows your account (or Sign in to Squeak...) instead of "Connected".</li><li>A warning with Restart appears only when Squeak's service isn't running.</li><li>Clicking the project or workspace in a chat's header opens its dashboard.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.18.4</h4><ul><li>Sign in to your Squeak account in Settings &gt; Account (Zoho, Google or email). This Mac then appears in your account, and your iPhone or browser signed in to the same account joins it without a code. You're told each time, with Revoke; "Ask before adding my own devices" brings the code back.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
